# Dashing Bloodsucker: "Whenever an enchantment you control enters ... this creature gets +2/+0 and gains lifelink until end of
# turn." Bot1 casts the Bloodsucker in turn 1 (a 2/5 creature, not an enchantment: no trigger). In turn 2 Bot2 casts a Bad Moon, an
# enchantment under the opponent's control: no trigger, so the Bloodsucker (black, +1/+1 from either player's Bad Moon) is a
# 3/6 with no keyword. In turn 3 Bot1 casts its own Bad Moon (CR 603.6a): 2+1+1 = 4 power plus 2 from the trigger = 6, Toughness 7
# unchanged by the pump, and Lifelink. In turn 4 (Bot2's) the effect has ended (CR 514.2): 4/7, no keyword.

